# Copy to .env.test (gitignored — real credentials go there, never here) and
# fill in the values below. @medusajs/utils's loadEnv() loads .env.test
# first, then falls through to .env for every other var (dotenv doesn't
# overwrite keys already set), so nothing else needs to be duplicated here.
#
# medusaIntegrationTestRunner's ephemeral-database machinery
# (@medusajs/test-utils's database.js / medusa-test-runner-utils/
# postgres-template.js) does NOT read DATABASE_URL at all for its
# CREATE DATABASE/DROP DATABASE admin connection or its MikroORM
# schema-setup connection — confirmed directly by reading dist/database.js.
# It builds both from four discrete vars (DB_HOST/DB_USERNAME/DB_PASSWORD/
# DB_PORT), defaulting to localhost/empty/empty/5432 when unset — which is
# exactly why the suite failed with a raw node:net connection error before
# this file existed: nothing is listening on localhost:5432 in dev, and
# .env only ever defined a single DATABASE_URL connection string, never
# these.
#
# Neon's pooled endpoint (the "-pooler" host in .env's DATABASE_URL) goes
# through PgBouncer, which doesn't support CREATE DATABASE's session-level
# DDL — confirmed directly. Point these at the same Neon project/database,
# same credentials, with "-pooler" removed from the host, which does
# support it (also confirmed directly, including a real CREATE DATABASE /
# DROP DATABASE round trip).
#
# TLS is handled automatically by apps/backend/patches/
# @medusajs__test-utils@2.21.0.patch (already applied via pnpm-workspace.yaml)
# once DB_HOST isn't "localhost" — no separate sslmode var needed here.
DB_HOST=ep-xxxxxxxx.c-2.eu-west-2.aws.neon.tech
DB_USERNAME=neondb_owner
DB_PASSWORD=
DB_PORT=5432
